# Apply one motor-settings document.
#
# `apply_fields` names the fields the caller wants to change; every other field keeps
# the value the motor has right now. An empty list keeps the historical behaviour: the
# document is applied as-is, which is what a caller sending a complete document expects.
#
# This exists because MotorSettings cannot express "not provided": an omitted numeric
# field arrives as 0 and an omitted boolean as false, so a partial document used to zero
# the pulse widths and rotation ranges and disable the motor (PR-2319).
MotorSettings motor_settings
string[] apply_fields
---
bool settings_applied
bool settings_persisted
